item+ function crates/lattice-core/src/search.rs :: build_index_parallel :: pub fn build_index_parallel(buffer: &[u8], chunk_size: usize) -> LatticeIndex { :: Parallel index build — partition the buffer into chunks, scan each for delimiter boundaries, then merge. For very large phexts (>100MB) where the O(n) sequential scan becomes noticeable.  Currently unused — sequential build is ~30ms for 4.26 MB which is already below perceptual threshold. Included for future scaling. :: doc comment
item~ function crates/lattice-core/src/search.rs :: search_lattice :: pub fn search_lattice( buffer: &[u8], index: &LatticeIndex, pattern: &str, case_sensitive: bool, max_results: usize, ) -> Vec<SearchHit> { :: Search the lattice for a text pattern (single-threaded). Returns hits in document order (by coordinate). :: doc comment
item+ function crates/lattice-core/src/search.rs :: search_lattice_auto :: pub fn search_lattice_auto( buffer: &[u8], index: &LatticeIndex, pattern: &str, case_sensitive: bool, max_results: usize, ) -> Vec<SearchHit> { :: Auto-selecting search: picks serial or parallel based on data characteristics. This is what the editor should call. :: doc comment
item+ function crates/lattice-core/src/search.rs :: search_lattice_parallel :: pub fn search_lattice_parallel( buffer: &[u8], index: &LatticeIndex, pattern: &str, case_sensitive: bool, max_results: usize, ) -> Vec<SearchHit> { :: Search the lattice for a text pattern across all available cores.  Uses rayon's work-stealing thread pool. Each scroll is a work unit — scrolls are independent so there's zero contention. Results are collected per-thread then merged in coordinate order.  Falls back to serial for small lattices (< PARALLEL_THRESHOLD scrolls) where thread synchronization cost exceeds the parallelism benefit. :: doc comment
