Subject: fix(edit): cache the shell and harden HTTP responses

Public items: 5 added, 0 removed, 2 changed. Dependencies did not change. Code lines after this commit: 11844.

commit 1d875e1a3a9ed5c5d530bb3dcf123d2c1d51aba1
parent b52664676b3b684635aa8409b1371ca599674d71
author Cursor Agent <cursoragent@cursor.com>
date 1793347493 2026-10-30
item+ command src/bin/phext_edit.rs :: no-store :: command "no-store" :: A command named no-store. The program runs it when the user types this word on the command line. :: signature
item+ const src/oauth.rs :: CONTENT_SECURITY_POLICY :: pub const CONTENT_SECURITY_POLICY: &str = concat!( "default-src 'self'; ", :: Policy for the embedded editor and the public pages.  The shell is one HTML document: an inline script, an inline stylesheet, `onclick` attributes, and `style` attributes. A nonce or a hash does not cover event-handler or style attributes, so those would mean rewriting the shell. `unsafe-inline` stays for that reason. There is no `unsafe-eval`. Sign-in is a same-origin link to `/api/auth/...`, which 302s to Google or GitHub; top-level navigations are not restricted. `upgrade-insecure-requests` is added only when the browser connection is HTTPS, so a local `http://127.0.0.1` session keeps working. :: doc comment
item+ const src/oauth.rs :: HSTS_VALUE :: pub const HSTS_VALUE: &str = "max-age=31536000"; :: One year. Matches `deploy/nginx-edit.phext.io.conf`. No `includeSubDomains`: this host is `edit.phext.io`, and a future sibling name under that host should not be pinned by accident. :: doc comment
item~ struct src/oauth.rs :: Limiter :: pub struct Limiter { :: In-memory cap on sign-in attempts per client address, per ten minutes.  Counts OAuth start/callback and a bearer token the server rejected (the token box sends that secret as `Authorization` on the next API call). Anonymous 401s are not counted, so opening the signed-out page does not spend the budget. The address is `X-Real-IP` when nginx sets it from `$remote_addr`; otherwise the last `X-Forwarded-For` hop, which is the one a single reverse proxy appends. :: doc comment
item+ function src/oauth.rs :: forwarded_https :: pub fn forwarded_https(headers: &HashMap<String, String>) -> bool { :: Function forwarded_https takes headers: &HashMap<String, String> and gives back bool. :: signature
item+ function src/oauth.rs :: security_header_block :: pub fn security_header_block(https: bool) -> String { :: Function security_header_block takes https: bool and gives back String. :: signature
item~ function src/oauth.rs :: write_to :: pub fn write_to(&self, out: &mut impl std::io::Write) { :: Serialize as an HTTP/1.1 response with `Connection: close`.  Auth and session bodies stay `Cache-Control: no-store`. There is no `Access-Control-Allow-Origin`: the editor is same-origin only. :: doc comment
