item~ struct src/oauth.rs :: Editors :: pub struct Editors { :: Accounts allowed to use the editor once signed in.  The list starts from `PHEXT_EDITORS` (the operator's bootstrap list) and can grow at runtime: when an editor accepts a submission, the originator's account is admitted — appended here and, when a backing file is configured (see `Gate::load_editors_file`), to that file, so the admission takes effect immediately and survives restarts. Entries sit behind a lock because admission happens through `&Gate` while other requests are reading the list. :: doc comment
item+ function src/oauth.rs :: admit_account :: pub fn admit_account(&self, who: &str, email: &str) -> bool { :: Admit an account as an editor, effective immediately and persisted to the editors file when one is configured. Used when an editor accepts a submission: the originator joins the editors. :: doc comment
item+ function src/oauth.rs :: is_editor :: pub fn is_editor(&self, session: &Session) -> bool { :: Whether a session belongs to an approved editor. :: doc comment
item+ function src/oauth.rs :: load_editors_file :: pub fn load_editors_file(&self, path: &std::path::Path) { :: Load additional editor entries from a file (one per line) and make it the backing file for future admissions. The phext-edit server calls this with its default admitted-editors file when `PHEXT_EDITORS_FILE` is not set. :: doc comment
item+ function src/oauth.rs :: load_file :: pub fn load_file(&self, path: &std::path::Path) -> usize { :: Point the list at its backing file and load any entries already in it (one per line; blank lines and `#` comments are ignored, and a line may still carry several comma-separated entries). Entries the list already has are not duplicated. Returns how many were loaded. :: doc comment
item+ function src/oauth.rs :: session :: pub fn session(&self, headers: &HashMap<String, String>) -> Option<Session> { :: The signed-in session for a request, if any. In `--local` mode this is the synthetic local developer (never for a forwarded request), mirroring `session_view`; otherwise it is the cookie session. :: doc comment
item+ struct src/submissions.rs :: Submission :: pub struct Submission { :: A data shape named Submission. Its fields are: pub id: String; pub filename: String; pub who: String; pub email: String; pub name: String; pub submitted_at: i64; pub bytes: usize; pub scrolls: usize; pub status: SubmissionStatus; pub decided_by: String; pub decided_at: i64; pub curated_as: String. :: signature
item+ enum src/submissions.rs :: SubmissionStatus :: pub enum SubmissionStatus { :: A named choice named SubmissionStatus. It is one of: Pending; Accepted; Declined. :: signature
item+ function src/submissions.rs :: content :: pub fn content(dir: &Path, id: &str) -> Option<Vec<u8>> { :: The uploaded phext bytes for a submission. :: doc comment
item+ function src/submissions.rs :: count_scrolls :: pub fn count_scrolls(content: &str) -> Option<usize> { :: Count the populated scrolls in a phext text. Wrapped in `catch_unwind`: the text is user input, and a parser panic must become a rejection, never a crashed request. :: doc comment
item+ function src/submissions.rs :: create :: pub fn create( dir: &Path, filename: &str, who: &str, email: &str, name: &str, content: &str, ) -> Result<Submission, String> { :: Store a new pending submission. Validates the file name and the phext (non-empty, parseable) before anything touches disk. :: doc comment
item+ function src/submissions.rs :: get :: pub fn get(dir: &Path, id: &str) -> Option<Submission> { :: One submission by id, or None. Ids from the network are validated before they ever become a path. :: doc comment
item+ function src/submissions.rs :: list :: pub fn list(dir: &Path) -> Vec<Submission> { :: Every submission in the directory, oldest first. Unreadable or malformed entries are skipped, never fatal. :: doc comment
item+ function src/submissions.rs :: sanitize_filename :: pub fn sanitize_filename(raw: &str) -> Option<String> { :: Reduce an offered file name to a bare, safe `*.phext` name, or None when nothing usable remains. Directory parts are stripped, so `../../notes.phext` is just `notes.phext`. :: doc comment
item+ function src/submissions.rs :: set_decision :: pub fn set_decision( dir: &Path, id: &str, status: SubmissionStatus, decided_by: &str, curated_as: &str, ) -> Result<Submission, String> { :: Record an accept or decline. The caller decides the status rules (only a pending submission may be decided); this just persists. :: doc comment
