item~ struct src/mmap.rs :: MappedLattice :: pub struct MappedLattice { :: A phext document with copy-on-write editing.  The document may be a chain (a multiverse): several member phexts — universes — in one file. All read/write methods operate on the *active* universe (see `universe` / `set_universe`); a plain phext is a chain of one universe and behaves exactly as it always has. :: doc comment
item~ function src/mmap.rs :: save :: pub fn save(&mut self) -> io::Result<()> { :: Save to the backing file. Plain documents commit their staged transaction and checkpoint — the base file ends up holding exactly the merged document, as the original rewrite save did, and the staged batch was durable in the WAL on the way. Chain files stay read-only here, with the reason named. :: doc comment
