parent 58e597db95637bc1130e0c0a3a4e884632811d67
author Emise <emise@localhost>
date 1795098566 2026-11-19
item+ command src/bin/phext_edit.rs :: traversals :: command "traversals" :: A command named traversals. The program runs it when the user types this word on the command line. :: signature
item+ const src/traversals.rs :: MAX_Q_BYTES :: pub const MAX_Q_BYTES: usize = 64 * 1024; :: The largest `q` string a record may carry (64 KiB). A traversal is a list of addresses; this is a storage bound, not a grammar limit — the tour grammar itself is unbounded. :: doc comment
item+ struct src/traversals.rs :: Traversal :: pub struct Traversal { :: A data shape named Traversal. Its fields are: pub id: String; pub who: String; pub name: String; pub q: String; pub created: i64; pub updated: i64. :: signature
item+ function src/traversals.rs :: count_steps :: pub fn count_steps(q: &str) -> usize { :: How many steps of a `q` string parse under the tour grammar. :: doc comment
item+ function src/traversals.rs :: create :: pub fn create(dir: &Path, who: &str, name: &str, q: &str) -> Result<Traversal, String> { :: Store a new traversal for `who`. Validates name and `q` before anything touches disk. :: doc comment
item+ function src/traversals.rs :: get :: pub fn get(dir: &Path, id: &str) -> Option<Traversal> { :: One traversal by id, or None. Ids from the network are validated before they ever become a path. :: doc comment
item+ function src/traversals.rs :: list :: pub fn list(dir: &Path) -> Vec<Traversal> { :: Every traversal in the directory, oldest first. Unreadable or malformed entries are skipped, never fatal. :: doc comment
